From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] setupapi, cfgmgr32: device interfaces through the configuration manager

Programs find HID, audio, serial and USB devices by their interfaces; most
of the calls for it failed:

- CM_Get_Device_Interface_List(_Size) (A/W/_Ex): the size calls were
  FIXMEs returning CR_FAILURE and the lists "@ stub"s. They list the paths
  of a class's interfaces, the enabled ones or all of them
  (CM_GET_DEVICE_INTERFACE_LIST_ALL_DEVICES), or a device's;
  CR_BUFFER_SMALL when the buffer is short.
- SetupDiOpenDeviceInterface(A/W) (a FIXME): opens an interface by its
  path into a device information set, with its device.
- CM_Get_Device_Interface_Alias(_Ex) (FIXMEs and "@ stub"s) and
  SetupDiGetDeviceInterfaceAlias ("@ stub"): the interface of another class
  the same device has with the same reference string.
- CM_Get_Device_Interface_Property(_Ex)W (CR_CALL_NOT_IMPLEMENTED), and the
  missing CM_Set_Device_Interface_Property(_Ex)W,
  CM_Get_Device_Interface_Property_Keys(_Ex)W,
  SetupDiGet/SetDeviceInterfacePropertyW and
  SetupDiGetDeviceInterfacePropertyKeys: an interface's device instance,
  class, reference string and whether it is enabled, read-only; its own
  properties under its key (as a device's are), the friendly name falling
  back to what a driver wrote in its Device Parameters.
- CM_Register_Device_Interface and CM_Unregister_Device_Interface
  (A/W/_Ex, "@ stub"s).
- cfgmgr32.h: the CM_GET_DEVICE_INTERFACE_LIST_* and
  CM_NOTIFY_FILTER_FLAG_* flags and the declarations.

Gate: test/cmifaces-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit, test/cmifaces-probe.c).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_IFACE_ALL_LISTED, SG_MUTANT_NO_IFACE_INSTANCE,
SG_MUTANT_IGNORE_REFSTR (setupapi/devinst.c).
